This is a fork of https://github.com/syv-ai/qwen38-27b-rtx3090 (since renamed
syv-ai/HyperQwen), branched at commit bae2023ffc98753d337d2d2041784a277599a4c4. Like
upstream, it is licensed under the Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE. Upstream ships no
NOTICE file. This one records what the fork adds and where everything else comes from.

Upstream
  Everything not listed below is the work of the qwen38-27b-rtx3090 contributors (see
  git log): the launchers, the vLLM 0.28.0 patch series in patches/ (which carries
  backports of vLLM pull requests, Apache-2.0), the KVarN port in kvarn/ (KVarN by
  Huawei CSL, Apache-2.0), the model-preparation and drafter scripts, the benchmarks and
  the documentation.

Not in this repository
  The model weights, the drafter and vLLM are downloaded at setup time under their own
  licenses.

Added or changed by this fork (changed lines are marked "(fork)")
  README.md, NOTICE
      The notice of the fork, its credits, and a caveat on the Docker quick start.
  templates/qwen3.8-27b.jinja, bench/test_chat_template.py
      A chat template derived from that of Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B (Apache-2.0, Qwen team), as
      shipped in dbirks/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound: it adds the reasoning_effort level
      'focused', and takes max/high as xhigh and minimal/none as low instead of raising.
      The test checks that it renders like the original wherever the original works.
  single-user/start_qwen.sh, bench/test_launcher_args.sh, README.md,
  single-user/README.md, docs/thinking-levers.md, .env.example
      The REASONING_EFFORT knob that serves that template, its test and its docs.
  README.md, single-user/README.md, docs/gotchas.md, bench/api_smoke.py
      Corrections: thinking_token_budget works on vLLM 0.28.0's V2 runner, and
      bench/run_benchmarks.sh measures with thinking on.
  patches/think-penalty.patch, patches/series, bench/test_think_penalty.py
      A vLLM 0.28.0 patch (Apache-2.0, like vLLM) that subtracts think_penalty from a few
      reflection-marker tokens while the model is inside its reasoning, and its tests.
  single-user/start_qwen.sh, bench/test_launcher_args.sh, README.md,
  single-user/README.md, docs/thinking-levers.md, .env.example
      The THINK_PENALTY and THINK_PENALTY_WORDS knobs that apply the patch, their test and
      their docs.
